  "description": "Unipi 1.1 controller: 12 digital inputs, 8 relay outputs, 1 analog output, 2 analog inputs",
  "revision": 1,
  "source": "unipi-11-modbus-map.xlsx, Unipi knowledge base page https://kb.unipi.technology/en:hw:04-extensions:downloads",
  "sources": [
    {"title": "Unipi 1.1 Modbus map (unipi-11-modbus-map.xlsx)", "url": "https://kb.unipi.technology/_media/files:products:unipi1:unipi-11-modbus-map.xlsx", "note": "Sheets Registers, Coils and Description; listed on https://kb.unipi.technology/en:hw:04-extensions:downloads"}
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Configuration is not permanently saved: the Description sheet states it is set on each power-on. Defaults: counters 0, debounce 0 ms, outputs OFF.",
    "Multi-register values (counters, floats) are taken as big-endian (most significant register first), as in the other Unipi maps; the spreadsheet only says bit 0 is the LSB and bit 15 the MSB.",
    "The spreadsheet does not state the transport or default unit id, so the format defaults (tcp+rtu, unit 1) are kept.",
    "Coils repeat the relay outputs that also appear as bits of holding register 1.",
    "Analog Output 1 is documented as 'int16, 0..4000 ~ 0..10V': mapped as int16 with 0.0025 V per count and a 0-10 V write range. The unit of the analog input floats is not stated in the spreadsheet, so none is set.",
    "The counter of Digital Input 12 is a uint16 (one register) in the spreadsheet; the other counters are uint32."
  ],
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 0,
  "x_status": "official",
